B.ai6=new A.fD("1. Who we are","Tactivo is a football session-planning app operated by Tactivo Limited, company number 17373279, registered in England & Wales at 63 Carlton Road, Erith, DA8 1DX, United Kingdom. Contact us at info@tactivo.co.uk. By using Tactivo you agree to these terms.")
B.ail=new A.fD("2. Who can use it","You must be at least 16 to create an account. Tactivo is built for coaches, not for players: do not use it to store information about children or any other person.")
B.aii=new A.fD("3. Your account","Keep your password to yourself; you are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us straight away if you think someone else has access to it.")
B.aic=new A.fD("4. Sessions and drills","Session plans are assembled on your device from a library of coach-written drills. They are suggestions, not instructions. You are the coach: you decide what is safe and appropriate for the players in front of you, and you remain responsible for their safety, supervision and wellbeing.")
B.aif=new A.fD("5. Drills you write","Drills and notes you write stay yours. You give us permission to store them and show them back to you inside the app, and nothing more \u2014 we do not publish them or show them to other coaches.")
B.aiq=new A.fD("6. What you may not do","Do not use Tactivo unlawfully, do not try to break into or disrupt it, and do not copy the drill library out of the app to republish it elsewhere.")
B.aik=new A.fD("7. Cost","Tactivo is free to use. If we ever introduce paid features we will say so clearly beforehand, and anything you have already saved will stay accessible to you.")
B.aie=new A.fD("8. Ending it","You can delete your account at any time in Settings, which erases your data immediately. We may suspend an account that breaks these terms.")
B.aib=new A.fD("9. Our liability","Tactivo is provided as it is, without a promise that it will always be available or error-free. Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot be limited by law.")
B.ai7=new A.fD("10. Changes and law","We may update these terms and will change the date above when we do. They are governed by the law of England and Wales.")
B.avh=s([B.ai6,B.ail,B.aii,B.aic,B.aif,B.aiq,B.aik,B.aie,B.aib,B.ai7],t.J8)
B.ai5=new A.a4X(B.avh)
B.ai2=new A.NN(B.ai5,null)
B.aim=new A.fD("1. Who is responsible","Tactivo Limited, company number 17373279, registered in England & Wales at 63 Carlton Road, Erith, DA8 1DX, United Kingdom, is the data controller for the information described here. Contact us at info@tactivo.co.uk about anything in this policy.")
B.aip=new A.fD("2. What we collect","Your email address and password, stored securely; we never see it. Your profile: display name, username, and anything optional you add \u2014 photo, bio, location, phone number, coaching role, qualification, experience \u2014 and, if you answer it, how you heard about Tactivo. Your coaching content: session plans, drills, session dates, team settings, ratings, and the private notes you leave after a session.\n\nWe keep a small record of use: when you open the app, when you sign in, and a few points during first set-up \u2014 the moment, which app it was (iPhone, Android or web), a random identifier for this install and, once you have one, which account. Nothing else. The set-up steps happen before you have an account, so they carry the install identifier alone, which is not linked to you. If a 3D drill fails to load the app sends a problem report naming the fault, the drill, and your account if you are signed in; it contains nothing you wrote.")
B.aio=new A.fD("3. What we do not collect, and the email we send","Tactivo has no analytics tools, no advertising and no tracking across other apps or websites: we do not record which screens you open or which features you use, we do not track your location, and we collect nothing about players or anyone else. The sign-in token on your device keeps you signed in; it is not used to track you.\n\nWe do send email, through Resend, our email provider: sign-in codes and messages about your own sessions to every coach, and coaching tips and news only to coaches who ticked the box \u2014 untick it in Settings, or unsubscribe from any of those emails. For every email we record that it was sent, whether it arrived and whether a link in it was tapped. For tips and news only, we also record whether it was opened \u2014 a tiny image in the email tells us. We keep your time zone and country so it arrives at a sensible local hour. The same goes for phone notifications if you turn them on. We use this to decide which messages are worth sending.")
B.aig=new A.fD("4. Why we hold it, and on what basis","To give you the account and the app you asked for, and to send sign-in codes and messages about your own sessions: that is our contract with you, and you have to give us an email address for it \u2014 everything else is optional. Tips, news and phone notifications go out on your consent, which you can withdraw at any time in Settings without losing anything else. We rely on our legitimate interests for the small record of use, the problem reports, and measuring whether our messages work; keeping your data secure is our legal obligation. Which messages you get is chosen automatically from how you have used the app, but no computer decides anything about you that has a legal or similarly significant effect.")
B.ain=new A.fD("5. Who else sees it","Your coaching content is private to your account unless you send it to someone: other coaches cannot see your profile, your notes or your ratings, and they cannot find your sessions. Four suppliers run the service \u2014 Supabase holds the database, your account and your photo; Resend sends our email; OpenRouter runs the AI service in section 7; Cloudflare serves the page a link opens. Supabase holds the database in Ireland. Resend, Cloudflare and OpenRouter handle data in the United States or, for Cloudflare, wherever the reader is; each works under the standard contract clauses approved for transfers out of the UK and the EEA, and every supplier is bound by contract to protect it as this policy describes. If you sign in with Google or Apple, that company confirms who you are and tells us your email address. We never sell your data.")
B.aih=new A.fD("6. Sending a session to another coach",'When you tap "Send to a coach" we make a link and give it to you to send on. Anyone with the link can read it, with no account and no password, so send it to the people you mean to. It is not listed anywhere and we ask search engines not to index it, but it is not a secret.\n\nThe link carries the session title, the age group, how long it runs, how many drills are in it, and your first name unless you turn on "Share without my name". The drills travel only as references to our own library: a drill you wrote yourself is never sent, and nor is anything you typed on a library drill. Your email address, username, photo, notes and ratings never travel with a link.\n\n"Stop sharing" on the session or the drill takes back every link you have made for it, as does deleting the session or your account; a stopped link may still be readable for up to a minute. Every shared page has a "Report this link" line that emails us, and we take down links reported for good reason.')
B.aid=new A.fD("7. The one thing we send to an AI service",'When you describe a session in your own words \u2014 "midfield gets overrun" \u2014 that sentence is sent to OpenRouter, which runs a Google Gemini model, to work out which focuses you mean. That is all it does: it never picks your drills, which are chosen on your phone from the library built into the app. We send the sentence and nothing else \u2014 not your name, not your email, not your saved sessions, nothing identifying your account \u2014 and we do not keep it afterwards, only a count of how often you use it. If the service is unavailable your session is still built.')
B.aij=new A.fD("8. How long we keep it","Until you delete your account. Deleting it in Settings removes your account, profile, photo, sessions, drills and notes from our live systems immediately; encrypted backups age out within 30 days. There is no recovery, so export anything you want to keep first.")
B.ai9=new A.fD("9. Your rights","You can ask for a copy of your data, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to how we use it, or have it moved elsewhere. Where we rely on consent you can withdraw it at any time, and you can tell us to stop marketing to you at any time. Most of it you can change in the app; for anything else email info@tactivo.co.uk and we will respond within one month. If you are unhappy with our answer you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.")
B.ai8=new A.fD("10. Children","Tactivo is for adult coaches and you must be 16 or over to use it. It holds no information about players. If that ever changes we will update this policy and tell you before it does.")
B.aia=new A.fD("11. Changes","If we change this policy we will change the date above, and we will tell you in the app if the change is significant.")
